WEBVTT

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:03.330
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:07.450
I will never forgive you!

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:12.840
Witness my power, Playmaker!

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:16.340
I activate my Skill, Storm Access!

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:21.300
It's possible to use a 
Skill during a Master Duel?

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:26.040
Now give me back my body, Playmaker!

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:27.810
That won't happen!

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.410
Because I'll defeat you this turn!

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:32.710
Go!  Pulse Pressure!

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:44.280
Are you okay, Playmaker?

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:46.490
Soulburner!

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:49.960
The whole Wind World is destabilizing!

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:55.530
If we stay here, we'll be in trouble!

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:58.270
Let's use the escape program to log out!

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:04.040
Bohman...  And who is the 
one who controls him?

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:07.680
I swear I'll find out who!

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:30.320
Our lives aren't forever

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:37.130
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:44.410
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:50.980
Sharing hope for the future

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:57.750
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:04.990
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:11.670
I want to share your pain

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.370
He had the same memories as you?

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:47.110
Yeah.  During our duel, when he talked 
about the past, it was the same as mine.

00:02:47.110 --> 00:02:51.730
So he knows your past.  How?

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:55.320
He must've investigated me somehow.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:57.320
And in detail.

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:01.120
He even tricked me, his best friend.

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:03.560
He's a very troublesome opponent.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:08.930
But he's our only lead to retrieve 
Kusanagi's brother's memories.

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:12.040
But the gate has vanished.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:15.640
For now, we have to wait for it to reappear.

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:17.800
Sorry, Kusanagi.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:21.010
I couldn't find a lead.

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:24.270
Don't sweat it.

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:27.490
I'm just glad you came home safe.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:33.480
Because I still need you guys!

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:35.460
Look at that.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:40.220
I added a room to go to LINK VRAINS.

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:44.800
Because you two will be 
on more missions together.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:46.440
That room's for me?

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:47.270
Yeah.

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:53.740
By analyzing the data we acquired near 
the gate, we might learn something.

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:56.720
This'll take some work.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:02.720
I see.  A gate in the restricted area.

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:06.930
It must be related to the other Ignis.

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:09.740
Why didn't you tell us?

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:14.070
You were hired to capture 
Playmaker and his Ignis.

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:17.740
I'm not obligated to give you any other info.

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:23.090
With the gate gone, Playmaker won't show up.

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:27.320
But if the gate reappears, 
he'll definitely go there.

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:30.370
Any guarantee that the gate will reappear?

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:35.480
My company is analyzing the gate to find out.

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:38.460
The one working with Playmaker - Soulburner.

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:41.210
Any info about him?

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:45.680
Unfortunately, we have no specific info.

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:49.050
But we know he has an Ignis.

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:52.880
He must be a Lost Incident victim.

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:57.070
When Playmaker appears, I'll contact him.

00:04:57.070 --> 00:04:59.800
Be ready to go at anytime.

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:02.910
Sorry, but I'm not your pet.

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:06.380
I'll do what I want.

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:08.530
Wait, Blood Shepherd!

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:16.590
You'll have no complaints when I 
capture Playmaker and his Ignis.

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:22.630
Can you trust him?

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:25.060
As a hunter, yes.

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:41.160
Playmaker is after the 
stolen consciousness data.

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:43.720
Consciousness data?  Who's?

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:45.310
I don't know.

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:48.200
But since he went to the gate...

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:52.860
...there may be a link between the 
consciousness data and the Ignis.

00:05:56.400 --> 00:06:01.140
Playmaker will contact the 
other Ignis.  He is the key.

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:06.380
SOL Technologies' higher-ups 
will keep pursuing him.

00:06:06.770 --> 00:06:09.080
You're very worried.

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:11.430
I owe him big.

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:16.720
We just have to wait for the gate to 
reappear and Playmaker to show up.

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:21.190
If I could only get in touch 
with Playmaker directly.

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:23.560
By searching all of Den City?

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:25.460
That's impossible.

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:32.400
A long-time duelist, first-rate hacking 
skills, and knows a lot about the Hanoi.

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:34.040
Anyone come to mind?

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:35.950
Not at all.

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:38.400
Despite having lots of quirky traits.

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:46.170
His personality and speech in real life 
may not be the same in LINK VRAINS.

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:51.020
But a person's true nature doesn't change.

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:53.760
If he's nearby, we'll know.

00:06:56.950 --> 00:06:58.080
Hey!

00:06:58.080 --> 00:06:58.910
Hi.

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:05.000
Good morning, Zaizen.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:07.240
Good morning.

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:10.240
I transferred recently.  I'm Takeru Homura.

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:11.270
Hello.

00:07:11.270 --> 00:07:12.480
I see.

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:14.380
Good morning, Fujiki.

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:15.480
Good morning.

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:20.450
She's completely different 
than in LINK VRAINS.

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:25.190
Sigh...  I wish I could talk 
to her about our intense duel.

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:26.660
Don't do that.

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:28.940
I know.

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:30.940
Zaizen!

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:35.940
You haven't shown up at Duel Club lately!

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:37.340
I've been busy.

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:40.340
Cold as usual.

00:07:40.340 --> 00:07:43.340
Duel Club?  Maybe I'll check it out.

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:45.820
Nice, transfer student!

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:48.550
I, Naoki Shima, will train you!

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:49.680
You?!?

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:51.560
Hey, be respectful!

00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:55.150
Even Playmaker appreciated my talent!

00:07:55.150 --> 00:07:57.680
Right, Fujiki?

00:07:57.680 --> 00:07:58.650
Who knows.

00:07:58.650 --> 00:08:02.620
You saw our passionate friendship!

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:04.970
Playmaker's in the Duel Club?

00:08:04.970 --> 00:08:06.360
Umm, well...

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:08.420
Naoki Shima?

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:10.480
Oh, you mean Brave Max.

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:14.610
He did claim to be Playmaker's best friend.

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:17.230
I tried making him tell the truth, but...

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:19.390
Maybe not "best friends."

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:22.250
More like soulmates!

00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:26.760
Because when the Hanoi 
captured me, he saved me.

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:30.960
Then you've met Playmaker 
outside of LINK VRAINS?

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:36.560
I still feel the warmth of his hands.

00:08:37.150 --> 00:08:41.530
So if I follow Naoki Shima, 
I'll find Playmaker?

00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:43.480
Maybe.

00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:50.250
I'll test whether he's a duelist skilled 
enough for Playmaker to want to be his best friend.

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:51.610
Test?

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:56.650
He's a big fan of Blue Angel, right?

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:01.050
A Blue Angel event?

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:01.900
What?

00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:03.260
That's sudden!

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:06.240
A flash event!

00:09:06.590 --> 00:09:10.230
Tension climax!

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:17.270
If it isn't Playmaker's best friend.

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:24.640
The beautiful lady I met at Central Station!

00:09:25.070 --> 00:09:28.110
My name is Brave Max!

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:31.340
Oh yeah.  Your name's Max.

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:33.950
Did the bounty hunter try to get you?

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:38.970
Not at all!  Even though I'm yearning 
to put my skills to the test!

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:42.590
What if I'm one of the bounty hunters?

00:09:43.750 --> 00:09:45.030
I'm kidding.

00:09:45.030 --> 00:09:49.050
But if you want to test 
your skills, I'll duel you.

00:09:49.050 --> 00:09:50.230
You?

00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:54.710
Show me the skills of 
Playmaker's best friend.

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:59.800
I may look like this, but 
I don't duel impetuously.

00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:02.540
But if you really want to...

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:11.480
Let it be known that even though you're 
a beautiful lady, I won't show mercy.

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:12.860
Understand?

00:10:12.860 --> 00:10:14.330
I expect nothing less.

00:10:18.520 --> 00:10:19.600
Duel!

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:26.510
My turn!

00:10:26.510 --> 00:10:29.420
I summon Altergeist Silquitous!

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:36.880
Silquitous can return a different Altergeist

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:41.120
on my field and a card on 
your field to our hands.

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:44.580
And this effect can 
activate during your turn.

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:54.070
I wonder how Playmaker's best friend 
will duel against Silquitous's effect.

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:59.580
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:03.640
Impressive, beautiful lady.

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:07.540
You cautiously summoned 
a monster with 800 ATK.

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:11.120
However!  My name is Brave Max!

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:14.850
A rare duelist accepted by Playmaker!

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:17.460
Our bond is stronger than steel!

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:18.390
Hotter than magma-

00:11:18.390 --> 00:11:20.640
I already ended my turn.

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:21.860
Oh.  Right.

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:24.830
My turn!  I draw!

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:36.370
Let me see your skills.

00:11:37.180 --> 00:11:38.510
I win!

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:44.370
With this hand, I'll definitely win!

00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:48.040
For real?  I'll win this turn?

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:52.360
Are you watching, Playmaker?  I'll win!

00:11:52.360 --> 00:11:56.700
Here I go!  I summon Scrap Kong!

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:02.640
Scrap Kong's effect activates!

00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:05.870
When it's summoned, I destroy this card!

00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:14.500
I activate Green Baboon's 
effect from my hand!

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:19.320
When an effect destroys a 
Beast-Type monster on my field,

00:12:20.320 --> 00:12:23.430
I can Special Summon it by paying 1000 LP!

00:12:27.900 --> 00:12:29.260
I'm not done!

00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:33.000
I activate the spell card, Double Summon!

00:12:34.370 --> 00:12:37.700
I can Normal Summon twice this turn!

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:41.440
I summon another Scrap Kong!

00:12:43.690 --> 00:12:46.480
Due to its effect, I destroy this card!

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:53.480
I pay 1000 more LP to Special 
Summon Green Baboon from my hand!

00:12:53.480 --> 00:12:59.080
He instantly lost 2000 LP to 
get two monsters with 2600 ATK!

00:12:59.080 --> 00:13:01.430
That's quite a bold move.

00:13:01.910 --> 00:13:03.270
Not bad.

00:13:03.270 --> 00:13:09.730
A hero gives up life to become stronger!

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:13.470
Nailed it!  I'm awesome right now!

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:16.140
But what's he planning to do?

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:24.090
If he takes Silquitous's effect into 
account, he knows attacking isn't a good idea.

00:13:24.090 --> 00:13:29.180
You don't think I'll just attack, do you?

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:31.570
What's his strategy?

00:13:31.570 --> 00:13:34.660
I can't read him at all.

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:37.970
This is the climax!

00:13:37.970 --> 00:13:42.200
Appear!  My - the hero's - circuit!

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:45.400
Here it comes!

00:13:45.870 --> 00:13:47.430
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:51.500
The summoning conditions are 
two Level 5 or higher Beasts!

00:13:51.500 --> 00:13:56.460
I set two Level 7 Green 
Baboons in the Link Markers!

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:58.970
Circuit combine!

00:13:58.970 --> 00:14:00.290
Link Summon!

00:14:00.290 --> 00:14:05.260
Appear, Link 2 Metal Baboon, 
Ruffian of the Forest!

00:14:07.940 --> 00:14:13.200
It's only Link 2, but it has over 2000 ATK!

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:16.700
Now my victory is certain!

00:14:16.700 --> 00:14:19.670
Victory percentage max!

00:14:20.150 --> 00:14:22.410
Huh?  What does he mean?

00:14:22.410 --> 00:14:26.640
He doesn't see the trap card I set?

00:14:27.460 --> 00:14:30.240
She's stunned due to my greatness.

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:32.880
You shouldn't underestimate me!

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:35.890
No, it's not just my set card.

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:39.640
He's acting like he's ignoring 
Silquitous's effect.

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:45.540
Even if he didn't Link Summon, his 
two Green Baboons have 2600 ATK each.

00:14:45.540 --> 00:14:48.240
He could've dealt over 4000 damage.

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:50.740
He's up to something!

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:53.370
Or this is too foolish.

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:57.460
He's laughing.

00:14:57.460 --> 00:15:00.780
The duel has already reached its climax!

00:15:01.180 --> 00:15:06.780
Battle!  Metal Baboon attacks 
Altergeist Silquitous!

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:11.030
I activate the trap, Altergeist Camouflage!

00:15:11.590 --> 00:15:14.260
I equip this card on Silquitous!

00:15:17.720 --> 00:15:22.060
Now your monsters can't attack Silquitous!

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:30.660
When I activated my trap card, Altergeist 
Multifaker's effect activates from my hand!

00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:33.080
It Special Summons itself!

00:15:35.020 --> 00:15:37.810
When it's Special Summoned,

00:15:37.810 --> 00:15:43.320
I can Special Summon a different Altergeist 
from my deck in defense position.

00:15:43.450 --> 00:15:46.800
Come, Altergeist Marionetter!

00:15:49.050 --> 00:15:51.900
Altergeist Silquitous's effect activates!

00:15:52.920 --> 00:15:57.420
I return a different Altergeist 
on my field to my hand to return

00:15:57.420 --> 00:16:00.470
a card on your field to your hand.

00:16:00.470 --> 00:16:02.410
No no no.

00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:07.410
Metal Baboon is a Link Monster, 
so it doesn't return to my hand.

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:12.420
He's just dumb.

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:14.650
I knew Shima was...

00:16:14.650 --> 00:16:16.840
Now what will you do?

00:16:16.840 --> 00:16:18.680
Out of options?

00:16:19.180 --> 00:16:27.300
I return Altergeist Camouflage to my hand 
to return Metal Baboon to your Extra Deck.

00:16:30.510 --> 00:16:32.750
Metal Baboon!

00:16:32.750 --> 00:16:37.480
My perfect formula for victory!  Why?

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:41.680
This is too absurd to be allowed!

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:45.450
But I won't lose!

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:49.330
I end my turn!

00:16:49.330 --> 00:16:53.720
And the fun is still ahead!

00:16:54.080 --> 00:16:55.780
This was a failure.

00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:59.070
He's just a guy who's acting cool.

00:16:59.070 --> 00:17:02.430
All that climax nonsense.

00:17:03.140 --> 00:17:05.440
My turn.  I draw.

00:17:07.030 --> 00:17:09.020
This is bad.

00:17:09.020 --> 00:17:12.140
I have no monsters, so I'm wide open!

00:17:12.140 --> 00:17:17.840
Her monster will pummel 
me, and I'll totally lose!

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:20.180
Too embarrassing.

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:23.190
Even if I lose, I can't lose pathetically.

00:17:23.190 --> 00:17:25.940
Or else, I can't face Playmaker.

00:17:26.720 --> 00:17:30.050
You won't do something super uncool, right?

00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:33.930
Like attack me three times directly 
when I'm completely naked?

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:38.140
Of course not.

00:17:39.420 --> 00:17:40.870
She's wonderful.

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:46.110
Appear!  The circuit that connects 
to the unknown parallel universe!

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:52.320
I set Multifaker and Silquitous 
in the Link Markers!

00:17:53.880 --> 00:17:54.990
Link Summon!

00:17:54.990 --> 00:17:59.720
Appear, Link 2 Altergeist Hexstia!

00:18:07.670 --> 00:18:10.100
1500 ATK...

00:18:10.100 --> 00:18:12.520
I can survive that!

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:16.010
I bet you're thinking that 
you can survive 1500 ATK.

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:18.380
Gulp!

00:18:18.800 --> 00:18:25.150
Hexstia gains ATK equal to the original 
ATK of an Altergeist next to its link.

00:18:25.840 --> 00:18:29.710
Marionetter has 1600 ATK!

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:31.970
So it gains 1600.

00:18:34.080 --> 00:18:38.660
3100?  What am I supposed to do against that?

00:18:38.660 --> 00:18:41.270
You excessively lowered your LP to 2000.

00:18:41.270 --> 00:18:43.770
Because you were showing off.

00:18:44.110 --> 00:18:45.270
Battle!

00:18:46.170 --> 00:18:49.370
Altergeist Hexstia attacks you directly!

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:06.400
Instead of three attacks, I lost to one.

00:19:06.400 --> 00:19:08.830
Super embarrassing!

00:19:09.170 --> 00:19:14.800
Sorry for winning, Playmaker's best friend.

00:19:17.050 --> 00:19:18.890
That was a mistake.

00:19:18.890 --> 00:19:21.570
Sorry to waste your time.

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:22.960
It was expected.

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:25.700
But you still have something to do.

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:31.700
Why did I agree to hold an 
event to lure someone like him?

00:19:31.700 --> 00:19:34.020
That's a waste of time.

00:19:34.430 --> 00:19:38.310
Damn!  Sorry, Playmaker!

00:19:38.310 --> 00:19:41.630
I tarnished my best friend's reputation!

00:19:41.630 --> 00:19:45.460
Pathetic!  But I will change-

00:19:49.710 --> 00:19:52.300
30 minutes until the event!

00:19:53.180 --> 00:19:56.540
Here I come, Blue Angel!

00:19:57.340 --> 00:19:59.010
The gate appeared?

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:00.480
Look.  There it is.

00:20:01.020 --> 00:20:03.910
Last time, it was in the 
restricted area's lowest level.

